```

Each slot is 64 bytes (cache-line aligned), with the sequence number serving as both a validity marker and a position indicator. The head and tail indices are stored in persistent memory to survive power failures.

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical low-level memory management with thread-safety using atomic bit ops on a compact bitmap. A beginner-friendly yet realistic task for systems work.

## Key Concepts

- Fixed-size block pools
- Bitmap-based tracking
- Atomic CAS and memory order
